  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An electrical power supply has an internal resistance. It supplies a direct current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> to an external circuit for a time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span>. What is the electromotive force (emf) of the power supply?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{total energy transferred to the whole circuit}}{I\\times t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{total power transferred to the whole circuit}}{I\\times t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{total energy transferred to the external circuit}}{I\\times t}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{total power transferred to the external circuit}}{I\\times t}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
